---
description: Monorepo management rules and best practices
globs: pnpm-workspace.yaml,turbo.json,package.json
alwaysApply: false
---
# Monorepo Management Rules

<rule>
name: atlas_monorepo
description: Standards for maintaining a well-structured monorepo
filters:
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "(?:package\\.json|pnpm-workspace\\.yaml|turbo\\.json)$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)monorepo|workspace|turborepo|pnpm"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When managing the monorepo:

      ## Turborepo Configuration
      - Implement proper workspace setup
      - Use proper task configuration
      - Implement proper caching
      - Use proper dependency management
      - Follow Turborepo best practices

      ## PNPM Workspace
      - Implement proper package structure
      - Use proper dependency sharing
      - Implement proper versioning
      - Use proper script management
      - Follow PNPM best practices

      ## Code Organization
      - Implement proper package boundaries
      - Use proper module federation
      - Implement proper code sharing
      - Use proper build optimization
      - Implement proper testing strategy

examples:
  - input: "Adding a new package to the monorepo"
    output: "Package follows proper structure with appropriate dependencies and build configuration"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule> 